  "query_preview": "..\n\nWinter weather: cooler air will cause precipitation to change to\nsnow in the Crazy and Beartooth/Absaroka Mountains as early as\ntonight. Snow will continue at times into Monday. Accumulations\nshould reach 1-3\" along the Beartooth Pass with higher amounts of\n5-9\" elsewhere in the Beartooth and Crazy Mountains, mainly above\n8000 feet. Because of impacts to travel along the Beartooth Pass,\nissued a Winter Weather Advisory for that area from 10pm tonight\nto 6pm Monday.\n\nSunday: scattered showers and thunderstorms will be around (20-90%\nchance, greatest in western mountains) but with lower dewpoints\nand cooler air in the lower levels, instability will be lower,\nso severe thunderstorms are not expected this day.\n\nWind: It will be windy across much of the area north of the MT/WY\nborder on Sunday and again Monday, with a 700 mb low to our north.\nLook for wind gusts of 30-50 mph with the strongest gusts in the \nwestern foothills.\n\nOverall the trend for next week will be toward warmer and drier\nweather. 500 mb pattern and CSU machine learning outlooks do not\nsuggest a risk of severe thunderstorms Monday and Tuesday, but a \nlow risk of severe weather does exist for areas north and east of\nBillings Wednesday-Friday. Torgerson/RMS",
